{"Organization enable/disable/delete does not invalidate getForLogin cache - when an organization is disabled, enabled, or deleted, the getForLogin cache keys are never invalidated, leaving stale IDP IDs in the cache": 0.8643407821655273, "addIdentityProvider/removeIdentityProvider in org provider do not directly invalidate the login cache - they rely on indirect dependency through JPA delegate calling update(), which is fragile if JPA implementation changes": 0.3788219392299652, "NullPointerException in getLoginPredicate when IDP config map is null - idp.getConfig().get(OrganizationModel.BROKER_PUBLIC) is called without null-checking getConfig(), which could throw NPE if config is null": 0.5997001528739929, "Missing isEnabled() re-check in onlyRealmBrokers path after cache wrapping - the REALM_ONLY path does not include the same re-check that was added to ORG_ONLY and ALL paths, potentially showing disabled IDPs on login page": 0.8994514346122742}